<!--
  A replacement manifest for the `tapsell_mediation` Flutter module.

  The published one declares `package="ir.tapsell.mediation"`, which is the
  same namespace as Tapsell's own native library (`ir.tapsell:tapsell-flutter`).
  AGP 8 and later refuse to merge two modules that share a namespace, so the
  build dies in the manifest merger. Renaming the module's namespace alone is
  not enough - the legacy `package` attribute then disagrees with it, and AGP
  rejects that too.

  So the module gets a new namespace and this manifest, which is the published
  one minus the `package` attribute. Nothing else changes: the meta-data below
  is what the SDK reads its key from, and `TapsellMediationAppKey` is filled in
  from android/keys.properties.

  See the override in android/build.gradle.kts. If a future release of the
  plugin drops the `package` attribute, delete both.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <application>
        <meta-data
            android:name="ir.tapsell.mediation.APPLICATION_KEY"
            android:value="${TapsellMediationAppKey}"/>
    </application>
</manifest>
